<title>USA: Neiman Marcus Sept same-store sales rise.</title>
<headline>Neiman Marcus Sept same-store sales rise.</headline>
<dateline>CHESTNUT HILL, Mass. 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>October 5, 1996*     September 30, 1995     % Chg.</p>
<p> Total Revenues  212.4 million	$ 189.8$million   + 11.9%</p>
<p>Comparable</p>
<p> Revenues     $ 203.3 million	$ 189.8 million     + 7.1%</p>
<p>			 9 weeks ended</p>
<p>	     October 5, 1996*     September 30, 1995     % Chg.</p>
<p> Total Revenues  362.0 million	$ 323.8$million   + 11.8%</p>
<p>Comparable</p>
<p> Revenues     $ 347.7 million	$ 323.8 million     + 7.4%</p>
<p>		    *Fiscal year ends August 2, 1997.</p>
<p>The Neiman Marcus Group consists of three operating units: Neiman Marcus Stores, NM Direct and Bergdorf Goodman.  Harcourt General, Inc. owns approximately 59 percent of the outstanding common equity in The Neiman Marcus Group.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
